00:26:38.444 --> 00:26:39.484
Just get out.

00:26:40.620 --> 00:26:40.900
Two.

00:27:02.380 --> 00:27:04.300
You've got some answers this country needs.

00:27:04.680 --> 00:27:06.580
Anyway, we're only a few miles from the bunker.

00:27:07.050 --> 00:27:08.390
I wasn't going to let him stop us.

00:27:09.260 --> 00:27:10.380
Everybody get back in the Jeep.

00:27:11.370 --> 00:27:12.810
I said get back in the Jeep!

00:27:30.028 --> 00:27:32.028
You

00:28:07.804 --> 00:28:12.204
arrived without further incident at the camouflaged entrance of Bunker No. 6.

00:28:12.604 --> 00:28:14.504
which had been built to be bomb-proof.

00:28:14.780 --> 00:28:17.320
in the event of an all-out atom bomb war.

00:28:23.580 --> 00:28:25.580
The control panel's over there. Everything's marked.

00:28:26.140 --> 00:28:27.720
Shut the door. I'll meet you in the lab.

00:28:53.356 --> 00:28:54.856
on Mayday Channel One.

00:28:55.052 --> 00:28:55.772
Mayday Homer.

00:28:56.556 --> 00:28:57.396
Mayday, Homer.

00:28:57.612 --> 00:28:59.412
Disable Fox, Niner 6. Over.

00:29:00.604 --> 00:29:02.784
Mayday, Homer, to Abel Fox, Niner 6.

00:29:03.548 --> 00:29:04.328
Just a moment, sir.

00:29:04.892 --> 00:29:05.892
General Stone.

00:29:06.140 --> 00:29:07.900
It's Major J. He's on number six.

00:29:08.100 --> 00:29:08.860
And he got through all right?

00:29:09.040 --> 00:29:10.700
Yes, Major J, Dr. Lamont.

00:29:10.908 --> 00:29:12.048
Professor Penner and his daughter.

00:29:12.368 --> 00:29:12.648
Good.

00:29:12.988 --> 00:29:13.308
Go on.

00:29:15.612 --> 00:29:16.152
Make it your aim.

00:29:16.700 --> 00:29:17.700
Listen carefully, all of you.

00:29:18.268 --> 00:29:20.408
A worldwide state of extreme emergency exists.

00:29:21.052 --> 00:29:22.992
The federal government has been evacuated from Washington.

00:29:23.644 --> 00:29:26.164
Total military and scientific mobilization has been ordered.

00:29:27.452 --> 00:29:27.812
Temps.

00:29:28.060 --> 00:29:29.760
To negotiate with the invaders has...

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:30.260
Hopeless.

00:29:31.148 --> 00:29:33.948
Continuing efforts by the military to destroy the invaders is...

00:29:38.412 --> 00:29:39.752
Hold on, General. Be right with you.

00:29:44.908 --> 00:29:47.388
The Geiger counter shows high radioactivity outside.

00:29:48.652 --> 00:29:50.412
All of you, turn off those white switches, quick!

00:30:02.200 --> 00:30:02.900
We're all right now.

00:30:03.020 --> 00:30:05.320
Those switches are medically sealed, the bunkers.

00:30:05.380 --> 00:30:08.020
They get bomb proof, safe from almost anything.

00:30:08.590 --> 00:30:10.210
Why the high radioactivity outside?

00:30:10.680 --> 00:30:13.300
We'd hear or at least feel any nuclear explosion

00:30:13.300 --> 00:30:14.720
close enough to give a reading like that.

00:30:19.080 --> 00:30:21.780
Radioactivity is in constant up and down.

00:30:22.660 --> 00:30:25.100
Ticlic pulsation doesn't make any sense at all.

00:30:25.220 --> 00:30:29.260
As if the wind were blowing radioactivity in and out and in.

00:30:30.220 --> 00:30:32.740
There's a line of something going past one at a time.

00:30:33.960 --> 00:30:34.840
We'd better take a look.

00:30:35.150 --> 00:30:35.570
Look?

00:30:39.900 --> 00:30:42.280
Circuit TV wasn't affected by the jamming.

00:30:42.760 --> 00:30:57.800
Not yet they have it. They're looking.

00:31:01.564 --> 00:31:02.664
And that's the reason why.

00:31:04.604 --> 00:31:05.624
The Walking Dead.

00:31:05.980 --> 00:31:07.980
inhabited by the invisible enemy.

00:31:08.540 --> 00:31:11.160
had left their spaceship nearby...

00:31:11.228 --> 00:31:13.228
to search for the scientists.

00:31:15.260 --> 00:31:17.160
So far, it looks like they don't know the bunkers here.

00:31:17.884 --> 00:31:18.884
You were right, Major.

00:31:19.324 --> 00:31:22.564
The invaders occupying those dead bodies are highly radioactive.

00:31:26.940 --> 00:31:29.140
Able Fox, Niner 6, to Mayday Homer.

00:31:29.500 --> 00:31:30.000
Over.

00:31:30.990 --> 00:31:31.670
What happened, Major Jay?

00:31:32.500 --> 00:31:34.500
Invaders outside the bunker looking for us, sir.

00:31:34.640 --> 00:31:36.430
We picked them up with the Geiger counters.

00:31:36.860 --> 00:31:38.640
We've already discovered they're highly radioactive.

00:31:38.960 --> 00:31:43.920
Dr. Penner, Dr. Lamont, unfortunately, we can't give you any help.

00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:47.920
No one's been able to come up with a single clue as to how to stop the invaders.

00:31:48.080 --> 00:31:50.280
We don't know how you're going to do the job,

00:31:50.340 --> 00:31:53.010
but you must find some weapon to stop the invaders.

00:31:53.490 --> 00:31:58.290
Major Jay, you'll use Mayday S-O-X for your reports.

00:31:58.490 --> 00:31:59.810
Good luck to you.

00:32:00.670 --> 00:32:02.660
Good luck to all of us. Over and out.

00:32:03.800 --> 00:32:05.500
Roger, we'll go. Over and out.

00:32:09.290 --> 00:32:11.340
Heard him. Any ideas?

00:32:12.710 --> 00:32:14.910
Every scientist in the world must be working on this.

00:32:15.070 --> 00:32:17.670
How do they expect us to hold out long enough in this prison?

00:32:18.000 --> 00:32:20.140
Why, those things out there are practically breathing down our necks.

00:32:20.670 --> 00:32:23.150
We're all scared, Dr. Lamont. You're not alone.

00:32:24.260 --> 00:32:27.580
I'm sorry, but when I saw that farmer you killed walking past the bunker, I got...

00:32:27.580 --> 00:32:29.960
Well, Major, I don't see any point of your being insulting about it.

00:32:30.250 --> 00:32:32.290
Miss Penner, I'm in charge of this outfit.

00:32:32.570 --> 00:32:35.110
We've got a job to do, and we're going to do it now.

00:32:35.840 --> 00:32:38.180
Well, I'm sure that Dr. Lamont and my father realized that.

00:32:39.540 --> 00:32:42.300
Since this thing started, I've seen a lot of men crack up mentally,

00:32:42.500 --> 00:32:43.660
like that farmer out there.

00:32:44.890 --> 00:32:45.870
But we need you.

00:32:46.420 --> 00:32:48.500
You can't afford the luxury of cracking up.

00:32:50.880 --> 00:32:52.770
John, the major is right.

00:32:57.170 --> 00:32:58.170
We need sleep by tonight.

00:32:59.220 --> 00:32:59.900
The work can't stop.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:05.110
so we'll have to sleep in four hour shifts agreed agreed you're going to need your daughter sir not

00:33:05.680 --> 00:33:10.040
until she has to take some notes for us all right professor you'll find everything you need here

00:33:10.040 --> 00:33:22.030
if it isn't here it doesn't exist better you'll help me with supplies while the sabotage by the

00:33:22.030 --> 00:33:29.830
invaders went on in ever-increasing fury government building communicate

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:49.410
The nation's units, warehouses, army supply depots, railroad and air terminals were the victims of incendiaries, completely demoralizing the high commands of the armed services of every nation in the world.

00:33:52.050 --> 00:33:57.830
Mayday Homer to Abel Fox 9 or 6. Mayday Homer to Abel Fox 9 or 6.

00:34:02.270 --> 00:34:05.150
This is Abel Fox, Niner 6, Major J, over.

00:34:06.920 --> 00:34:08.840
Major General Stones, Dr. Penner there?

00:34:09.440 --> 00:34:09.860
Right next to him.

00:34:11.730 --> 00:34:12.830
We can't hold out here much longer.

00:34:14.240 --> 00:34:15.040
Any progress there?

00:34:16.460 --> 00:34:17.520
Nothing definite, sir.

00:34:18.380 --> 00:34:19.660
Well, maybe this will be of some help.

00:34:21.160 --> 00:34:23.140
We've been able to establish a definite pattern.

00:34:24.300 --> 00:34:27.480
The invaders either have no weapons of their own, which is unlikely,

00:34:28.050 --> 00:34:29.970
or the ones they do have won't work in our...

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:37.100
General, this is Dr. Penner. What about the sabotage, the explosion, the fire?

00:34:38.040 --> 00:34:40.180
All created by our own weapons against us.

00:34:41.400 --> 00:34:45.230
Then their only weapon, actually, is the fact that they're invisible.

00:34:46.550 --> 00:34:50.020
That's right. Dr. Harkov in Moscow believes there must be a weakness

00:34:50.020 --> 00:34:54.300
in the molecular structure of their basic materials, their metals, in Earth's atmosphere.

00:34:55.160 --> 00:34:58.900
It might also indicate a weakness in the molecular structure of their bodies.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:01.000
Thanks, General. This might help.

00:35:04.760 --> 00:35:06.480
We'll report back in two hours, sir.

00:35:07.120 --> 00:35:07.260
Right.

00:35:08.060 --> 00:35:08.460
Burnout.

00:35:11.580 --> 00:35:12.360
Lamont and your daughter?

00:35:13.660 --> 00:35:15.400
They've only had a little over an hour's rest.

00:35:15.900 --> 00:35:18.080
I want to work on this new aspect alone for a while.

00:35:22.390 --> 00:35:28.440
Dr. Fenner, do you still feel the same way about the testing of nuclear weapons?

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:31.740
Major, I think I do.

00:35:33.060 --> 00:35:35.920
If the Lord wills it, we'll come out of this alive.

00:35:36.690 --> 00:35:39.010
Then perhaps the nations of the world will realize

00:35:39.010 --> 00:35:42.140
it's possible to work together, as they're doing now,

00:35:42.690 --> 00:35:45.850
instead of trying to destroy each other with nuclear bombs.

00:35:55.950 --> 00:35:56.630
I didn't sleep much.

00:35:57.100 --> 00:35:58.020
I thought I heard the radio.

00:35:59.100 --> 00:35:59.980
General Stone had...

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:05.970
something for us. Your father thought it might be a lead. Can I help? Uh-uh. He wants to work

00:36:05.970 --> 00:36:18.140
on it alone. You hate my guts, don't you? You killed a man in cold blood this morning. I keep

00:36:18.230 --> 00:36:29.980
seeing his face. So do I. Way through Korea. Probably killed a lot of men. I never saw

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:39.180
their faces dropping a bomb from a plane isn't quite so personal can i make you some coffee no

00:36:39.940 --> 00:36:47.370
thanks i've had enough already it's either your father or the man with the shotgun i had to make

00:36:47.370 --> 00:36:57.660
a choice perhaps i was wrong about john too what about the way you insulted him you had to make

00:36:57.660 --> 00:36:58.360
that choice, too.

00:37:00.280 --> 00:37:01.680
Well, he was going off the deep end.

00:37:03.070 --> 00:37:03.750
Worked, didn't it?

00:37:04.280 --> 00:37:05.960
At least it was better than slugging him.

00:37:08.960 --> 00:37:11.020
I majored in psychology at college,

00:37:11.040 --> 00:37:13.850
but I'll take a few lessons from you, Major.

00:37:14.900 --> 00:37:15.740
Yeah, yeah, sure.

00:37:17.350 --> 00:37:18.770
If there's anything left of this world

00:37:18.770 --> 00:37:20.590
after we get out of here, we'll talk about it.

00:37:22.810 --> 00:37:25.010
Lamont, you two majoring in each other?

00:37:26.290 --> 00:37:27.190
Lamont and I...

00:37:27.190 --> 00:37:27.490
Phil!

00:37:31.850 --> 00:37:39.220
get john for me please hurry find something i'm not sure it'll work it's going to take some courage

00:37:39.220 --> 00:37:55.050
to find out major one of us will have to leave the bunker is it adam i told you of the device

00:37:55.080 --> 00:37:59.490
used by the invader who contacted me uh the thing that made the metal or visible

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:07.060
Yes. Well, since this morning, I've been working on the theory that the device may have projected a ray of some sort.

00:38:07.380 --> 00:38:09.830
Now, only two theories seem to make any sense.

00:38:10.090 --> 00:38:16.300
That the ray changed the light spectrum, or that it temporarily changed the molecular structure of the ore itself.

00:38:17.830 --> 00:38:22.580
Dr. Penner, you said one of us should have to leave the bunker. Why?

00:38:23.210 --> 00:38:24.090
I'm getting to that, Major.

00:38:24.780 --> 00:38:29.970
Before I can test either of the theories, we'll have to capture one of the invaders to test it.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:33.000
That's a pretty tall order.

00:38:33.510 --> 00:38:34.310
We have no choice.

00:38:34.810 --> 00:38:37.330
We'll have to bring one of the creatures into the bunker.

00:38:38.500 --> 00:38:40.660
Adam, how can you possibly capture something you can't see?

00:38:41.150 --> 00:38:43.830
There's a fire foam spray among our equipment.

00:38:44.440 --> 00:38:46.960
Can you convert it to handle an acrylic spray?

00:38:47.230 --> 00:38:48.130
Acrylic spray?

00:38:48.980 --> 00:38:51.660
A liquid plastic mixed with a catalyst

00:38:51.660 --> 00:38:55.380
that covers and solidifies on contact, forms a hard shell.

00:38:56.460 --> 00:38:58.870
Stuff used to mothball Navy equipment and tanks.

00:39:00.600 --> 00:39:03.140
If I can convert the gun, then what?

00:39:03.800 --> 00:39:08.900
I believe the invisible creatures enter a dead body through the pores of the skin.

00:39:09.730 --> 00:39:11.330
Sort of an osmosis process.

00:39:11.550 --> 00:39:15.430
And the acrylic spray will seal the body so the invader can't get out?

00:39:15.910 --> 00:39:18.350
It's only a theory. I said it might not work.

00:39:18.530 --> 00:39:19.950
Adam, we can't take such a chance.

00:39:20.090 --> 00:39:21.510
One of those things might escape here in the bunker.

00:39:21.610 --> 00:39:22.390
None of us would be saved.

00:39:22.470 --> 00:39:24.970
John, well, maybe there's some other way.

00:39:25.050 --> 00:39:26.090
Maybe there's something else.

00:39:26.090 --> 00:39:28.310
If there is another way, we haven't got time for it.

00:39:28.840 --> 00:39:29.840
All right, Dr. Penner.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:32.140
You get on with the spray, I'll try and convert the gun.

00:39:33.860 --> 00:39:38.420
Phyllis, they've no right to put you in such danger.

00:39:39.620 --> 00:39:40.540
Haven't they, John?

00:39:48.690 --> 00:39:50.830
By 11.30 of the first night,

00:39:51.740 --> 00:39:54.880
the nations of Earth were close to total defeat.

00:39:56.470 --> 00:39:59.980
All through the night, Dr. Penner and Dr. Lamont...

00:40:00.190 --> 00:40:07.570
labored to manufacture the acrylic formula meanwhile major jay with the help of phyllis

00:40:07.570 --> 00:40:17.170
penner converted the fire foam gun so that it could use the liquid plastic by dawn they had

00:40:17.170 --> 00:40:25.960
succeeded remember if i don't make it you'll have to try again they won't quit now you asked

00:40:25.960 --> 00:40:29.020
about John and me, we're just all friends, that's all.

00:40:30.350 --> 00:40:31.050
Glad I asked.

00:40:37.400 --> 00:40:37.760
All clear.

00:40:39.360 --> 00:40:39.920
All clear.

00:40:41.580 --> 00:40:42.400
Okay, open the door.

00:40:43.830 --> 00:40:45.510
There's enough radiation out there to kill you.

00:40:45.950 --> 00:40:46.690
Please be careful.

00:40:47.050 --> 00:40:47.770
This suit's tough.

00:40:47.870 --> 00:40:48.390
I'll be all right.

00:42:16.120 --> 00:42:18.500
truck to get to him. Look.

00:42:30.820 --> 00:42:58.410
He's leaving if he gets far enough away. We won't need the truck. Oh, I'm all right

00:43:00.030 --> 00:43:02.050
The spray gun won't work. It's not fast enough.

00:43:06.390 --> 00:43:08.990
However, I still think the acrylic spray is the answer.

00:43:10.420 --> 00:43:13.530
When I hit the body with it, the invader took off fast.

00:43:13.980 --> 00:43:14.860
He was afraid of it.

00:43:15.140 --> 00:43:16.320
But how can we use it?

00:43:17.590 --> 00:43:19.860
Well, that depends on Lamont's nerves.

00:43:20.670 --> 00:43:22.350
Look, Major, you've been trying to...

00:43:22.350 --> 00:43:24.130
All right, all right. Take it easy. Relax.

00:43:24.900 --> 00:43:27.080
I need your help. I'm asking for it.

00:43:27.560 --> 00:43:29.960
My life's going to be in your hands, and I don't want to go into...

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:32.120
this thing with two strikes against me.

00:43:32.520 --> 00:43:33.740
Well, what do you want me to do now?

00:43:33.960 --> 00:43:34.480
I'll tell you in a minute.

00:43:35.440 --> 00:43:37.740
Dr. Penner, can you make up a large amount of this spray?

00:43:38.360 --> 00:43:38.820
We might.

00:43:39.180 --> 00:43:39.600
All right.

00:43:39.700 --> 00:43:41.620
We're going to have to move fast now after what's happened.

00:43:43.180 --> 00:43:45.620
Have any of you wondered why I wasn't killed by that invader out there?

00:43:46.060 --> 00:43:48.060
You said the invader was frightened by the spray.

00:43:48.690 --> 00:43:49.230
That's right.

00:43:49.500 --> 00:43:51.340
The spray was more important than I was.

00:43:52.200 --> 00:43:56.140
He probably went back to his spaceship to report we were getting pretty close to something

00:43:56.140 --> 00:43:57.060
that might bother them.

00:43:58.770 --> 00:43:59.970
That'll mean they'll double their...

00:44:00.060 --> 00:44:01.800
forces to find this bunker and knock it out.

00:44:02.160 --> 00:44:04.420
But it will also mean the entire area around here

00:44:04.420 --> 00:44:05.520
will be filled with these creatures.

00:44:05.880 --> 00:44:07.620
That's why only two of us will leave the bunker.

00:44:07.800 --> 00:44:09.280
Phyllis and Dr. Penner will stay here.

00:44:09.630 --> 00:44:10.770
Then if we don't get back,

00:44:11.110 --> 00:44:12.390
there'll be somebody left to keep working.

00:44:12.620 --> 00:44:13.980
But there's only one radiation suit.

00:44:14.100 --> 00:44:14.820
That's all we need.

00:44:15.200 --> 00:44:16.480
You'll stay in the cab of the truck.

00:44:16.640 --> 00:44:17.240
It's protected.

00:44:18.300 --> 00:44:18.940
As you say.

00:44:19.340 --> 00:44:20.800
All right, let's get busy on the spray.

00:44:21.210 --> 00:44:22.490
I'll explain what I have in mind.

00:44:25.370 --> 00:44:28.110
Knowing the invader's spaceship must be in the area,

00:44:28.860 --> 00:44:29.980
Major J chose...

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:33.260
the likely spot to set his trap for catching one of the enemy.

00:44:43.480 --> 00:44:48.880
Okay, this looks like the spot around here, but not too close.

00:44:49.870 --> 00:44:51.720
Remember, don't get out of the truck.

00:44:52.500 --> 00:44:56.420
I understand. Major, there's one thing you haven't said.

00:44:57.470 --> 00:44:57.670
Yeah?

00:44:58.750 --> 00:44:59.970
You're actually making yourself...

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:08.300
the bait and the trap to catch one of the creatures no better way to go fishing no i don't all right

00:45:08.300 --> 00:45:15.200
stay with that geiger counter in case i get company signal with that horn and fast one long one short

00:45:38.190 --> 00:45:44.430
A deep hole had been dug, and now it was being filled with the acrylic liquid.

00:45:45.490 --> 00:45:48.310
The next step was to set a noose beneath the liquid,

00:45:49.140 --> 00:45:53.630
for once the acrylic hardened, the encased corpse would have enormous weight.

00:46:14.750 --> 00:46:19.830
The plan now was to lure one of the walking dead into the area where the pit had been dug.

00:46:20.590 --> 00:46:26.840
A direct attack by Major J was the quickest, though most dangerous, method of baiting the invader.

00:48:02.780 --> 00:48:03.660
They're coming. Get ready.

00:48:03.840 --> 00:48:04.300
All right, Dad.

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:30.460
Are you all right?

00:48:30.660 --> 00:48:31.160
I'm okay.

00:48:31.440 --> 00:48:32.040
Get your father.

00:48:32.140 --> 00:48:33.400
I want to get our friend into the chamber.

00:48:33.600 --> 00:48:33.940
Hey, DJ!

00:48:35.680 --> 00:48:35.780
DJ!

00:48:37.480 --> 00:48:38.660
They're outside, all around us.

00:48:38.740 --> 00:48:39.480
I saw them on the monitors.

00:48:39.720 --> 00:48:41.100
They probably followed the truck.

00:48:48.120 --> 00:48:49.280
Just smashed down the door.

00:48:50.490 --> 00:48:51.150
Take it easy.

00:48:51.350 --> 00:48:53.190
This place was built to stand an atom blast.

00:48:53.870 --> 00:48:54.470
Come on, help me.

00:49:11.550 --> 00:49:13.350
The pressure will crack that stuff on the body?

00:49:13.650 --> 00:49:15.930
It can crush anything, not built to withstand it.

00:49:16.740 --> 00:49:19.400
All right. When the acrylic coating on the body splits,

00:49:19.810 --> 00:49:21.730
we'll be turning an invader loose in the chamber,

00:49:22.540 --> 00:49:24.960
if we've caught one. Let's find out.

00:49:25.160 --> 00:49:26.080
Pressure, Dr. Spinner.

00:49:50.570 --> 00:49:51.710
We've got one of those things in here.

00:49:51.850 --> 00:49:54.170
A mob of those dead men right outside.

00:49:55.710 --> 00:49:58.610
Going out in that truck, they couldn't have followed us back to the bunker.

00:49:58.930 --> 00:49:59.650
John, shut up!

00:50:01.530 --> 00:50:02.710
Another point, Dr. Penner?

00:50:39.850 --> 00:50:41.490
Looks like we caught ourselves an invader.

00:50:42.670 --> 00:50:44.210
The rest is up to you, Dr. Penner.

00:50:45.470 --> 00:50:45.790
Wait.

00:50:56.890 --> 00:50:57.590
Left the body.

00:50:58.600 --> 00:50:59.980
Let's hope we can keep it locked up in that chair.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:00.260
chamber.

00:51:30.380 --> 00:51:34.490
Your people are being destroyed, country by country.

00:51:36.270 --> 00:51:38.490
My unit has already received reports.

00:51:39.810 --> 00:51:41.950
Your nations are considering surrender.

00:51:44.890 --> 00:51:45.470
You're lying.

00:51:46.070 --> 00:51:48.570
You can check with your commanders for the truth.

00:51:49.360 --> 00:51:51.140
If they'd surrendered, you'd have said so.

00:51:53.920 --> 00:51:58.830
You will surrender to me now, be spared.

00:51:59.730 --> 00:51:59.910
Look.

00:52:00.030 --> 00:52:04.940
friend you're the prisoner and as long as we have you to work over we still have a chance

00:52:08.420 --> 00:52:19.940
dr penner continue on with the tests you will die as all the rest of you shall die dr penner

00:52:19.940 --> 00:52:26.820
and dr lamont began immediate experiments in a desperate effort to make the invader visible to

00:52:26.820 --> 00:52:29.760
the human eye the vast

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:34.820
The scientific knowledge of the two men was put to the test in a race against time.

00:52:35.500 --> 00:52:42.300
For they knew that with every moment of failure, thousands more people all over Earth would die.

00:52:46.400 --> 00:52:48.100
Time was running out for the defenders.

00:52:48.940 --> 00:52:52.120
The world was nearing the end of its ability to fight back.

00:52:52.860 --> 00:52:54.540
For this was the third day.

00:52:56.120 --> 00:52:59.970
By midnight, the human race on Earth would...

00:53:00.030 --> 00:53:15.730
cease to exist still trying to battle down the garage door now they gave that up but they're

00:53:15.730 --> 00:53:21.380
still out there probably trying to figure a new way to get at us thing in the chamber

00:53:21.380 --> 00:53:27.370
knows we're trapped he knows we can't get out of here alive if we surrender you think they'd let

00:53:27.370 --> 00:53:29.960
us live maybe maybe we won't

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:34.540
know if we don't try. All our experiments have failed. What good is waiting? We're not giving up

00:53:34.540 --> 00:53:41.010
or do you two go along with it? Major, we've tested everything. Light rays,

00:53:41.170 --> 00:53:45.340
every shade on the spectrum. Chemicals, mechanical devices,

00:53:45.870 --> 00:53:51.440
nothing. We can't make it visible. We can't hurt it. I asked you a question.

00:53:51.970 --> 00:53:57.090
Do you agree with Lamont or don't you? I don't. I'm too weary to think straight anymore.

00:53:57.310 --> 00:53:59.940
Look, we can't hold out here forever. Let's take the road.

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:00.720
See what happens.

00:54:01.010 --> 00:54:02.110
Look, the three of you.

00:54:02.290 --> 00:54:04.250
That thing in the chamber is bluffing.

00:54:04.800 --> 00:54:09.840
The very fact that he's offering us our lives if we stop the test proves that we're on to something.

00:54:10.620 --> 00:54:12.320
And he's afraid we're gonna find out.

00:54:12.540 --> 00:54:13.280
You're a fool.

00:54:13.720 --> 00:54:15.380
We're no closer down than we were an hour ago.

00:54:15.540 --> 00:54:17.880
Do what you like.

00:54:18.440 --> 00:54:19.280
I'm taking the offer.

00:54:19.400 --> 00:54:20.400
I'm letting that thing out of the chamber.

00:56:00.560 --> 00:56:01.340
What then?

00:56:01.460 --> 00:56:01.840
The creature.

00:56:02.290 --> 00:56:04.310
You heard the alarm bell on the radiation counter.

00:56:04.750 --> 00:56:07.530
Well, the explosion and concussion made the creature react.

00:56:08.090 --> 00:56:08.910
Nothing else has.

00:56:09.430 --> 00:56:09.870
React?

00:56:10.190 --> 00:56:12.440
We've been looking the wrong way for our answer.

00:56:12.800 --> 00:56:15.250
It isn't in light waves or chemicals.

00:56:15.490 --> 00:56:16.970
The answer is in sound.

00:56:17.760 --> 00:56:18.540
Sound, John.

00:56:18.960 --> 00:56:19.380
Sound?

00:56:20.050 --> 00:56:21.170
To create sight?

00:56:21.660 --> 00:56:27.750
You said the device used by that creature that came to your house caused a humming sound.

00:56:28.240 --> 00:56:28.560
Yes.

00:56:29.300 --> 00:56:29.980
The sound...

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:34.380
It was low-key to our ears, but the device must have used sonic rays,

00:56:35.110 --> 00:56:40.210
sound vibrations that created resonance with the basic molecular structure of the metal ore.

00:56:41.540 --> 00:56:44.140
And that resonance caused visibility.

00:56:45.340 --> 00:56:46.580
I just hope it isn't too late.

00:56:53.990 --> 00:56:57.230
Sound is the answer. It certainly reacted during the explosion.

00:56:58.360 --> 00:56:59.980
Listen, when the chemicals...

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:01.320
and that flask hit the panel.

00:57:02.040 --> 00:57:04.970
It caused a short circuit, jumped the breakers

00:57:04.970 --> 00:57:06.710
and blew up our entire air conditioning

00:57:06.710 --> 00:57:07.710
and filtering system.

00:57:08.190 --> 00:57:09.730
Luckily, our radio's still intact.

00:57:10.660 --> 00:57:11.720
How long can the air last?

00:57:11.900 --> 00:57:12.880
About an hour and a half.

00:57:13.650 --> 00:57:15.010
Then we're gonna have to open the air vents.

00:57:15.520 --> 00:57:17.940
We'll be sitting ducks for what's waiting for us outside.

00:57:18.360 --> 00:57:20.080
Major, I want to apologize.

00:57:20.340 --> 00:57:21.140
It's all right, forget it.

00:57:21.880 --> 00:57:23.360
Look, if you think sound is the answer,

00:57:23.520 --> 00:57:24.840
you better make sure and fast.

00:57:44.750 --> 00:57:51.220
One doesn't generate enough sound, both probably break our own eardrums.

00:59:37.520 --> 00:59:42.860
Major, there's your weapon. It not only makes the invader visible, it destroys them as well.

00:59:43.470 --> 00:59:44.870
Could the army turn these out in a hurry?

00:59:45.240 --> 00:59:48.120
I could give headquarters all needed details in a matter of minutes.

00:59:48.280 --> 00:59:48.820
Good. Come on.

00:59:53.290 --> 00:59:56.030
Mayday, Homer. This is Abel Fox, Niner 6. Over.

00:59:56.920 --> 00:59:57.780
Abel Fox...

01:00:25.690 --> 01:00:29.970
You could use the jamming signal to find the spaceship by tracking it.

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:31.800
on the direction finding radio in the truck.

01:00:33.080 --> 01:00:35.170
Yeah, that'd be our only chance

01:00:35.170 --> 01:00:36.810
to get your information to General Stone.

01:00:36.990 --> 01:00:39.070
Yes, but what about the invaders waiting for us outside?

01:00:39.810 --> 01:00:41.010
We're gonna crash right through.

01:00:41.480 --> 01:00:44.000
And if you have any special prayers for a job like this,

01:00:44.080 --> 01:00:44.960
you better start saying.

01:00:45.310 --> 01:00:53.260
If you let us out, get to the transmitter.

01:00:53.920 --> 01:00:55.360
When the jamming signal goes off,

01:00:55.480 --> 01:00:56.620
call the general in a hurry.

01:00:57.120 --> 01:00:57.840
Good luck, Major.

01:00:58.600 --> 01:00:59.880
Don't miss with a sound.

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:02.200
It's the only chance you have against radiation.

01:01:21.510 --> 01:01:23.570
Okay, Dr. Benner, open her up.

01:02:50.480 --> 01:02:59.310
Spaceship was the only key to the location of the ship the directional finding equipment on the truck

01:03:00.030 --> 01:03:06.390
by Dr. Lamont had to use this key successfully or all hope would be gone.

01:03:11.600 --> 01:03:17.650
Slowly but surely, the radio jamming led the truck to the immediate area of the invisible

01:03:17.650 --> 01:03:19.820
ship used by the invaders.

01:05:09.240 --> 01:05:11.540
Mayday Homer, this is Abel Fox 6. Come in, please.

01:05:12.210 --> 01:05:14.330
Mayday Homer to Abel Fox 9 or 6.

01:05:14.900 --> 01:05:17.440
Come in, Abel Fox 9 or 6. Come in, please.

01:05:41.960 --> 01:05:45.790
In the United Nations building in New York, a special meeting was called.

01:05:47.570 --> 01:05:53.450
Present were Dr. Penner, his daughter, Major J, and Dr. Lamont

01:05:54.020 --> 01:05:57.200
to receive grateful thanks from the countries of the world.

01:05:57.790 --> 01:05:59.720
Earth had been on the brink of disaster.

01:06:01.280 --> 01:06:06.340
But out of the Holocaust of war, in which a dictatorship of the universe had been defeated,

01:06:07.460 --> 01:06:08.800
a lesson had been learned.

01:06:10.720 --> 01:06:18.540
The nations of the world could work and fight together, side by side, in a common cause.
